// the same exit code through a linked binary rather than the JIT.
//
// worth its own case because the two get there differently: under `run` the JIT'd code calls libc `exit`
// and takes *echoc itself* down with it, so the status the suite sees is the program's only because
// nothing intervenes. Here it is an ordinary process exit.

echo 1;
std::env::exit(3);
